#{[{:activity/first-step {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186074538} :activity/id #uuid "b07ed8c4-8ba9-5778-a813-94fb9ccc2843" :activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050295 :topic/id #uuid "3d7bd7bf-6970-5ce8-8de1-27d53b866227" :topic/math-academy-id 510} :activity/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186074538 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186074992 :tutorial/content "Consider the right triangle below.\n\n![](images/cd/cd056cb2c92d918412778089c0744525fb676a79047b0e779161c68db8210d54.png)\n\nWe know that\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}\\sin A = \\frac{BC}{AC}, & \\cos C = \\frac{BC}{AC}, \\\\ \\cos A = \\frac{AB}{AC}, & \\sin C = \\frac{AB}{AC}\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nConsequently,\n\n$$\n\\sin A = \\cos C\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n\\cos A = \\sin C\n$$\n\nNow, let\n\n$$\nm\\angle A =\\theta\n$$\n\nThen, since $\\angle A$ and $\\angle C$ are complementary, we have\n\n$$\nm\\angle C = 90^\\circ - \\theta\n$$\n\nand we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\sin θ &= \\cos (90^{∘} - θ) \\\\\n\\cos θ &= \\sin (90^{∘} - θ)\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn other words,\n\n- the sine of an angle equals the cosine of its complement, and\n- the cosine of an angle equals the sine of its complement.\n\nSine and cosine are known as **cofunctions**. The latter is called **co**sine to indicate that it is the **co**function of sine." :tutorial/id #uuid "3b432c9c-d757-5975-9b24-999b2bce5a31" :tutorial/math-academy-id 2456 :tutorial/title "Introduction"} :step/id #uuid "c97a3887-eade-5923-b47f-6b98202badf5" :step/math-academy-id 10997 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186074577}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186074539 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186073672 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186073616 :question/id #uuid "83830700-8d9b-5205-8f3e-764247162987" :question/math-academy-id "e-3266"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "4b7cb13a-a561-5a95-a87c-5d2f2a59b08e" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050661} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050928}] :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186074025} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186074026}] :knowledge-point/title "Expressing a Trigonometric Ratio as a Cofunction of a Complementary Angle"} :step/id #uuid "5b219563-3ca8-59a2-ad6d-59b8d4876029" :step/math-academy-id 10998 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186074540}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186074540 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186073673 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186073617 :question/id #uuid "320908eb-adaf-5516-9810-a4fae4dc8f38" :question/math-academy-id "e-3268"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "52f46344-b7c0-51a1-918c-aaac34dd5c40" :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186074253} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186074254} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186516777} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186550010}] :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Value of a Variable Satisfying a Cofunction Equality"} :step/id #uuid "ea4cf402-26be-57c6-a0f8-f6d5d0730154" :step/math-academy-id 10999 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186074541}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186074541 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186073674 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186073618 :question/id #uuid "27b53e09-978d-5d78-aa3f-ad9c780adfeb" :question/math-academy-id "e-3270"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "c1ec0eb3-ea8e-5783-b6a2-dc7128709f71" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049496}] :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186074079} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186074255} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186233293} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186516787} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186516799} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186549964}] :knowledge-point/title "Expressing a Trigonometric Ratio With a Linear Expression Angle as a Cofunction of a Complementary Angle"} :step/id #uuid "5c679c15-81dd-565b-89b0-c0e2d65c49af" :step/math-academy-id 11001 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186074542}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186074542 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186073675 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186073619 :question/id #uuid "bd79dabb-70aa-58d8-9273-f15fed5d65cd" :question/math-academy-id "e-3271"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "b653137f-4991-5388-b34d-8573c58c0841" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048673}] :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186074081} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186074106} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186549955}] :knowledge-point/title "Solving for a Variable Given Two Angles and a Cofunction Equality"} :step/id #uuid "7d64db21-880b-5b14-9446-eb999ee3cd8e" :step/math-academy-id 11002} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186074577 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186075000 :tutorial/content "So far, we know that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\sin θ &= \\cos (90^{∘} - θ), \\\\\n\\cos θ &= \\sin (90^{∘} - θ)\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the above properties, we can also derive cofunction properties for secant and cosecant. We start with\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\sec θ &= \\frac{1}{\\cos θ} \\\\\n&= (1)/(\\sin (90^{∘} - θ)) \\\\\n&= \\csc (90^{∘} - θ)\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nBy the same reasoning, we can show that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\csc θ &= \\sec (90^{∘} - θ)\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo we have deduced that secant and **co**secant are also cofunctions. To summarize:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\sec θ &= \\csc (90^{∘} - θ), \\\\\n\\csc θ &= \\sec (90^{∘} - θ)\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, by similar reasoning, it's possible to show that tangent and **co**tangent are cofunctions. Their cofunction relationships are\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\tan θ &= \\cot (90^{∘} - θ), \\\\\n\\cot θ &= \\tan (90^{∘} - θ)\n\\end{aligned}\n$$" :tutorial/id #uuid "04166248-ef12-5aa7-b46b-1a077920d60c" :tutorial/math-academy-id 2562 :tutorial/title "Reciprocal Functions of Complementary Angles"} :step/id #uuid "60e93782-7e78-571a-affc-f9bf9070f1e5" :step/math-academy-id 11755 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186074539}}] :activity/title "Trigonometric Functions of Complementary Angles" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :activity.type/lesson} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186073937}] [{:activity/course {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186046647} :activity/first-step {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186516953} :activity/id #uuid "2f13de55-4b4a-58a1-86bc-d11cf8ac70ea" :activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050295 :topic/id #uuid "3d7bd7bf-6970-5ce8-8de1-27d53b866227" :topic/math-academy-id 510} :activity/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186516924 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186516787 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "28286d6d-ad07-57e3-bf30-df2a9fc9669f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\operatorname{cot}⁡(\\theta +{38}^{∘})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186516195} {:answer/id #uuid "3e419048-16ff-5c66-ae89-db3a66c0e04b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\operatorname{tan}⁡({38}^{∘}-\\theta )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186516234} {:answer/id #uuid "6c996574-91a9-51e8-9312-f04c34295651" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sin}⁡({38}^{∘}-\\theta )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186516351} {:answer/id #uuid "bf651374-36d8-557f-b681-3dc03d4228d6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sec}⁡({38}^{∘}-\\theta )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186516518} {:answer/id #uuid "db5ab455-9105-51dc-b743-f8595cf1ed86" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sec}⁡(\\theta +{38}^{∘})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186516573}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186516573} :answer-field/id #uuid "7dda5fed-8473-5945-9921-a17a8674675e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186516710}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "2741d45a-fa16-53e2-880b-c02211a343a6" :question/math-academy-id "q-121635" :question/problem "Express $\\operatorname{csc}⁡({52}^{∘}-\\theta )$ as a cofunction of a complementary angle." :question/worked-solution "We know that the cofunction of $\\operatorname{csc}⁡\\theta $ is $\\operatorname{sec}⁡\\theta ,$ and the angle complementary to ${52}^{∘}-\\theta $ is \n\n$$\n{90}^{∘}-({52}^{∘}-\\theta )={90}^{∘}-{52}^{∘}+\\theta =\\theta +{38}^{∘}.\n$$\n\n \n\n So we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{csc}⁡({52}^{∘}-\\theta )=\\operatorname{sec}⁡({90}^{∘}-({52}^{∘}-\\theta ))=\\operatorname{sec}⁡(\\theta +{38}^{∘}).\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "7b98e68e-3539-59ad-9433-947e7808f548"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186516947 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186516799 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "249bd755-b9fc-5059-a4cc-054bc42e9314" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sec}⁡({59}^{∘}-\\theta )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186516182} {:answer/id #uuid "a2f9945e-67bd-552a-92a0-da62f3ed7aec" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sec}⁡({31}^{∘}-\\theta )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186516448} {:answer/id #uuid "e568a46e-9865-52b5-95e3-a68f91b5f928" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\operatorname{tan}⁡({59}^{∘}-\\theta )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186516590} {:answer/id #uuid "eddd4ec4-631c-5919-aeb3-fe7717bba038" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sin}⁡({31}^{∘}-\\theta )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186516605} {:answer/id #uuid "fc4b055c-aeb5-5d2a-b243-457b5c94d048" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sin}⁡({59}^{∘}-\\theta )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186516639}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186516639} :answer-field/id #uuid "5d9dfd76-7e56-51fc-b4c9-69b55120139b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186516688}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "48f83c42-2b91-552c-8245-857f1b1c658c" :question/math-academy-id "q-54180" :question/problem "Express $\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\theta +{31}^{∘})$ as a cofunction of a complementary angle." :question/worked-solution "We know that the cofunction of $\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta $ is $\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ,$ and the angle complementary to $\\theta +{31}^{∘}$ is \n\n$$\n{90}^{∘}-(\\theta +{31}^{∘})={90}^{∘}-\\theta -{31}^{∘}={59}^{∘}-\\theta .\n$$\n\nSo we have\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\theta +{31}^{∘})=\\operatorname{sin}⁡({90}^{∘}-(\\theta +{31}^{∘}))=\\operatorname{sin}⁡({59}^{∘}-\\theta ).\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "ae182013-f585-5116-920c-7437b922e562" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186516986}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186516953 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186074081 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8bc448ef-ad7d-573d-9492-1e1fa503989b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186070355} {:answer/id #uuid "9687551b-7554-5709-ab37-c37ccd8eb982" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186070356} {:answer/id #uuid "de51a6d2-c8d5-5050-a5b7-7f7ecc5db40c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "13" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186070357} {:answer/id #uuid "0de35427-4700-5455-aeef-e3d6cb0e1fba" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186070358} {:answer/id #uuid "12fdcb2b-c21e-552b-8b9d-a52c607d5cf5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "11" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186070359}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186070359} :answer-field/id #uuid "1712deff-6406-55d7-b884-b4d5e3627df7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186070354}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "5f4e61a7-f26a-56bc-8378-0113cfde8291" :question/math-academy-id "q-23396" :question/problem "If $m∠A=(5x+16)^{∘}$ and $m∠B=(x+8)^{∘},$ find a value of $x$ that satisfies $\\operatorname{cot}⁡A=\\operatorname{tan}⁡B.$  Suppose that both $∠A$ and $∠B$ are acute." :question/worked-solution "If both angles are acute and $\\operatorname{cot}⁡A=\\operatorname{tan}⁡B,$ then the angles $∠A$ and $∠B$ must be complementary, and we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(5x+16)^{∘}+(x+8)^{∘} & ={90}^{∘} \\\\ (6x+24)^{∘} & ={90}^{∘} \\\\ 6x+24 & =90 \\\\ 6x & =66 \\\\ x & =11.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "b6a5d555-12ef-5ca1-a482-6a77ec3f6c76" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186516947}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186516986 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186516777 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1d6260fb-52da-585b-8762-43ddb0c85bd9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{65}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186516167} {:answer/id #uuid "52894601-4ce1-5150-accd-ddb12bf8ce0a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{39}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186516284} {:answer/id #uuid "95595f2a-9508-56a1-9b79-2e80f73d9cfe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{28}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186516420} {:answer/id #uuid "c879ab7d-d2e0-5cdf-a36d-49043d561722" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{49}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186516537} {:answer/id #uuid "f0745c84-f316-5a12-9678-2861eb0bf75f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{32}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186516609}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186516284} :answer-field/id #uuid "987f7db7-dd4a-52e2-baa4-bf058dad8795" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186516726}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "177a5181-a104-5ae5-8d0b-29a1b6bce482" :question/math-academy-id "q-67541" :question/problem "Determine a value of $x$ satisfying the equation $\\operatorname{tan}⁡{51}^{∘}=\\operatorname{cot}⁡x.$" :question/worked-solution "Since the tangent of an angle equals the cotangent of its complement, we have\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{tan}⁡{51}^{∘}=\\operatorname{cot}⁡({90}^{∘}-{51}^{∘})=\\operatorname{cot}⁡{39}^{∘}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $x={39}^{∘}$ satisfies the given equation."} :step/id #uuid "fe87cad6-ab86-5015-a4aa-04da945279b2" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186516924}}] :activity/title "Trigonometric Functions of Complementary Angles" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :activity.type/review} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186516091}] [{:activity/course {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186046647} :activity/first-step {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186550079} :activity/id #uuid "85248f71-9a91-59f8-abfd-a331609b85d7" :activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050295 :topic/id #uuid "3d7bd7bf-6970-5ce8-8de1-27d53b866227" :topic/math-academy-id 510} :activity/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186550026 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186549955 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "196e30cc-dd4b-56ea-a0b6-1806966dbb09" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "13" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186549367} {:answer/id #uuid "201f479f-c986-5031-a33c-dbafb94414b7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186549379} {:answer/id #uuid "6244bb6c-d4f3-5dc9-b931-a8f929d8ca7e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "16" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186549510} {:answer/id #uuid "80eac182-2d21-5af9-acc3-8bc865bbba69" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "17" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186549555} {:answer/id #uuid "ec8b7699-f736-58a7-a627-e8c62a400d67" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "14" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186549750}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186549750} :answer-field/id #uuid "3954b075-3cbd-547a-ab25-a35f014d84a8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186549827}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "3a13b69c-0da2-5493-86d2-76c8bc977240" :question/math-academy-id "q-76841" :question/problem "If $m∠A=(3x+1)^{∘}$ and $m∠B=(4x-9)^{∘},$ find a value of $x$ that satisfies $\\operatorname{cot}⁡A=\\operatorname{tan}⁡B.$  Suppose that both $∠A$ and $∠B$ are acute." :question/worked-solution "If both angles are acute and $\\operatorname{cot}⁡A=\\operatorname{tan}⁡B,$ then the angles $∠A$ and $∠B$ must be complementary, and we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(3x+1)^{∘}+(4x-9)^{∘} & ={90}^{∘} \\\\ (7x-8)^{∘} & ={90}^{∘} \\\\ 7x-8 & =90 \\\\ 7x & =98 \\\\ x & =14.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "0a6e5921-a726-56cb-bfef-3f735f7f9c34"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186550074 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186549964 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "232770a9-261e-542e-9bec-2581712671f9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\operatorname{tan}⁡({63}^{∘}+\\theta )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186549387} {:answer/id #uuid "2bbc56e7-2aaf-5e66-b87f-ea39cdff55ec" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\operatorname{tan}⁡({117}^{∘}-\\theta )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186549412} {:answer/id #uuid "41ef6204-53b5-57d1-aff2-d8612595549f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sin}⁡({63}^{∘}+\\theta )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186549454} {:answer/id #uuid "b0afc406-fee9-55f5-92dc-507c9f3aad2f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\operatorname{tan}⁡({117}^{∘}+\\theta )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186549646} {:answer/id #uuid "ffea38d3-c884-5870-9640-07170f484d8c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sin}⁡({117}^{∘}-\\theta )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186549795}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186549387} :answer-field/id #uuid "555314da-5e88-5538-91a3-29bd66ea2f89" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186549835}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "5cb3bde9-32a4-52cd-9e8b-d6d4c061a2e8" :question/math-academy-id "q-76838" :question/problem "$\\operatorname{cot}⁡({27}^{∘}-\\theta )=$" :question/worked-solution "We know that the cofunction of $\\operatorname{cot}⁡\\theta $ is $\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\theta ,$ and the angle complementary to ${27}^{∘}-\\theta $ is \n\n$$\n{90}^{∘}-({27}^{∘}-\\theta )={90}^{∘}-{27}^{∘}+\\theta ={63}^{∘}+\\theta .\n$$\n\nSo we have\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cot}⁡({27}^{∘}-\\theta )=\\operatorname{tan}⁡({90}^{∘}-({27}^{∘}-\\theta ))=\\operatorname{tan}⁡({63}^{∘}+\\theta ).\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "85c20f4a-b465-5c04-9a70-5f8524fd68f3" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186550026}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186550079 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186550010 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "37e36ca0-728d-5777-83e2-15bb76b35468" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{31}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186549429} {:answer/id #uuid "38c3d6a9-5ad0-509f-b053-9f0356aa4fcf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{20}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186549431} {:answer/id #uuid "8718d378-3671-57d6-8abd-ace85ee02878" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{29}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186549568} {:answer/id #uuid "afe422a8-d707-5f59-ab2f-273daf6ca9d9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{22}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186549645} {:answer/id #uuid "f35e6b7b-5124-511d-b409-af45d7700f1c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{25}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186549771}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186549568} :answer-field/id #uuid "f1136b74-6034-598a-adbe-d3d54ab43b8c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186549915}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "ebda143e-32ac-588d-bb70-63d0142c284b" :question/math-academy-id "q-54165" :question/problem "Find a value of $x$ satisfying the equation $\\operatorname{cot}⁡{61}^{∘}=\\operatorname{tan}⁡x.$" :question/worked-solution "Since the cotangent of an angle equals the tangent of its complement, we have\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cot}⁡{61}^{∘}=\\operatorname{tan}⁡({90}^{∘}-{61}^{∘})=\\operatorname{tan}⁡{29}^{∘}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $x={29}^{∘}$ satisfies the given equation."} :step/id #uuid "936a37e0-3b01-55f9-87dc-10c8d8e898c3" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186550074}}] :activity/title "Trigonometric Functions of Complementary Angles" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :activity.type/review} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186549309}]}
